From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 91/91] web-app: requests link in the chat list, quiet group
 requests

Request the chat list with core's DC_GCL_NO_REQUESTS so contact requests
no longer get their own rows. Core's requests link is rendered by the
archive-link component (forum icon, "Request" label, the request count
as its counter, no "mark all as read" menu); clicking it opens a
Requests view that reuses the archive view's header (back button and
title) and lists the chats via the `is:request` query. Keyboard
next/previous chat skips every special chat ID, not only the archive
link.

Notifications for group contact requests are dropped in
flushNotifications, so a cloned group earns no alert. 1:1 requests
still notify: missing a real first message is worse than one ping.
